    <string name="chat_desc">What complex topic shall we illuminate today?</string>
    <string name="user_msg_1">Can you help me solve this integration problem step by step?</string>
    <string name="calculus_ii">Calculus II</string>
    <string name="ai_response_intro">Of course! This is a classic case for Integration by Parts combined with a trigonometric substitution. Let\'s break it down into manageable steps:</string>
    <string name="step_1_title">Identify the components:</string>
    <string name="step_1_formula">Set u = x and dv = sin(x) dx.</string>
    <string name="step_2_title">Apply the formula:</string>
    <string name="step_2_desc">Use ∫u dv = uv - ∫v du. Differentiating u gives du = dx, and integrating dv gives v = -cos(x).</string>
    <string name="step_3_title">Reassemble:</string>
    <string name="step_3_desc">This results in -x cos(x) - ∫(-cos(x)) dx, which simplifies further as we integrate the cosine term.</string>
    <string name="final_answer_title">FINAL ANSWER</string>
    <string name="final_answer_formula">-x cos(x) + sin(x) + C</string>
